to-arthur-brock-source : List Word
to-arthur-brock-source = lines-of (cons "# Arthur Brock"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik Jain's work, hyperactivity, exists because of yours. He says so in these words: “There is a man named Arthur Brock who I respect deeply and in so many ways set me exactly down this path. this would not exist without him. it is a continuation of his life's work. Eric Harris-Braun as well.” His paper says the same"
  (cons (cite hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source "(Part III, hyperactivity is the theory of knowledge graphs)")
  (cons ". You hold full credit for every construct of yours the system builds on: receptors, semantic trees, self-describing protocols, membranes, the agent-centric stance, and currencies as records of currents. Nothing here is offered as a replacement for Ceptr. It is Ceptr's design stated in a mathematics that can carry it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work saw that the field still does not"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field treats meaning as something a reader brings to bits. Data is syntax, its interpretation lives in whichever program happens to read it, and interoperability is bought one brittle API at a time. Ceptr refused that. Data carries its own meaning: a semantic tree whose every node is labeled with what it is, protocols that describe themselves, and receptors that exchange signals whose structure and sense travel with them. Semtrex, regular expressions over semantic trees, follows: once meaning is in the data, recognition works at every layer of a protocol stack. Ceptr describes itself as a fractal computing stack of self-described protocols built on a flow-centric view of reality. That is a statement about what computing is."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Holochain carried the same insight into distributed systems. The 2018 white paper you wrote with Eric Harris-Braun and Nicolas Luck names the error of blockchains exactly: global sameness mistaken for consensus. Each agent keeps its own hash-chained source chain, validates by rules the application declares, and joins a shared table where an entry's key is the hash of its value. Membranes say who may enter. Agreement is local and earned, not global and imposed."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The MetaCurrency work holds the same idea in economics. Currencies are Records of Currents (2020) says a currency is a record of a flow that would otherwise vanish. The flow, not the token, is the thing."
  (cons ""
  (cons "These are one thought: meaning, agency and value are flows, and a system should record them faithfully rather than flatten them into one global state read by one privileged interpreter."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up from it"
  (cons ""
  (cons (cite to-everyone-source "Hyperactivity, in Avik's words,") (cons "is Wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon, with cubical type theory at its core"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Semantic trees become types.** The paper puts it this way: Ceptr's symbols and structures become types, matching on meaning becomes elimination over a type and its identities, and two structures meaning the same thing are related by an equivalence along which everything carries across"
  (cons (cite hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-source "(Part III)")
  (cons ". Operations and their laws are transported together across such an equivalence"
  (cons (cite s4-p2 "(§4)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Self-describing protocols become typed interactions.** A process is stated against a signature of commands and their response types"
  (cons (cite s7-6-p3 "(§7.6)")
  (cons ", and a handler supplies the interpretation of its requests in a particular world"
  (cons (cite s10-p6 "(§10)")
  (cons ". A protocol edit, its proof, the residual parser, the emitted artifact and the rollout are operations on one represented computation, and two protocol versions can coexist"
  (cons (cite s10-11-p7 "(§10.11)")
  (cons ". Avik's earlier work with Gašper Ažman at Citadel Securities, a language for arbitrary protocols that generated optimal reactive parsers, is the same substance from practice"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Agent-centric validity.** Holochain refused global sameness and let each agent validate. The paper states the same stance: an invariant over a global state no participant can see, proved conserved by every allowed local transition"
  (cons (cite s10-3-p8 "(§10.3)")
  (cons ", and a peer proves an action safe for every state compatible with its own observations without possessing the global state"
  (cons (cite s10-3-p12 "(§10.3)")
  (cons ". Another participant, with a different history, yields a different family of interpretations"
  (cons (cite s1-p21 "(§1)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Content addressing is the store.** Holochain's table keys entries by the hash of their value. Hyperactivity's store identifies every definition by its content, and a name is only a view of it"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Records of currents.** A currency records a flow that would otherwise vanish. In the paper, the full history is recovered without loss when the observed value and the history with its evidence are retained"
  (cons (cite s1-p10 "(1.2)")
  (cons ", and a retained result records every observation it rests on, including absence"
  (cons (cite s10-1-p2 "(§10.1)")
  (cons ". The event is gone; the witness remains and can be read."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Membranes.** A response from the outside world is never replayed as though it were a pure lookup: what crosses the boundary of a computation stays distinct from what was computed inside it"
  (cons (cite s10-1-p5 "(§10.1)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Hyperactive Receptivity"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik has a name for the work he means to bring you: Hyperactive Receptivity. In the workflow its node formalizes Ceptr's protocols in the language"
  (cons (cite metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-source "(Part III, cubically receptive)")
  (cons "; his intent is every construct of Ceptr and every key statement of its design as constructions with proofs, culminating in a hyperactive receptor. He found Ceptr through the Ceptr Revelation document. Among its comments from people following the project, one mentioned homotopy type theory, and he believes that may be how HoTT first entered his thinking: the cubical foundation of hyperactivity is in that sense a reply to Ceptr's own community."
  (cons ""
  (cons "He holds Ceptr to be the only system so far that attempts rational intelligent design of computing as a whole. Hyperactivity is his attempt to finish that design with a logic strong enough to hold all of it at once. Read it as Ceptr given a proof theory: the places where it is strongest are the places your design pointed to first, and the credit for that pointing is yours."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Holochain: Scalable Agent-Centric Distributed Computing, alpha white paper (Harris-Braun, Luck, Brock, 2018), https://holochain.org/documents/holochain-white-paper-alpha.pdf"
  (cons "- Currencies are Records of Currents (Arthur Brock, MetaCurrency Project, 2020), https://medium.com/metacurrency-project/currencies-are-records-of-currents-f4c6cdc809be"
  (cons "- Ceptr source repository, https://github.com/zippy/ceptr"
  (cons "- Ceptr wiki, https://ceptr.decko.org"
  (cons "- Ceptr overview, MetaCurrency Project, https://medium.com/coinsolidation/ceptr-994609b1b911"
  (cons "- Arthur Brock, biography (RiseUP), https://www.weriseup.com/biography/arthurbrock"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Parts I and III, the definitions linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
